WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.280
Are ya ready, kids?

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:02.140
No!

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.900
I can't heeeeaar yoouuuuuu~

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:05.280
No!!

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.280
..maybe now?

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.640
I SAID NO! :|

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.640
(Several Bad Puns Later)

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.020
pretty please?

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:11.720
NO!

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.380
OOOOH--

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.920
-kay then, lets just start the episode.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:18.520
*film theory boss intro music*

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.480
Hello internet! Welcome to Film Theory.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.720
The show that may not be absorbent or yellow,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.900
but is definitely full of holes.

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:43.120
Now, as much as I love the exposing dark, sinister side of innocent cartoons,

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.800
SpongeBob doesn't seem like it's hiding that many skeletons in its closet.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:49.000
I mean, SpongeBob is a hard working employee,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.380
who makes enough to provide for himself with the career that he enjoys.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.600
And unlike all those orphaned Disney characters, has two loving parents.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.100
Wait, those are his parents?

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.440
Yeah, THOSE are his parents...

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.500
And no, he isn't the son of two cookies.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.180
Unlike the bright, yellow, and rectangular SpongeBob,

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.820
Harold and Margret Squarepants had their appearance designed after real life sea sponges.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:14.240
Given that the show's creator Stephen Hillenburg is a marine biologist,

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.040
it's a cool nod to the real life science of undersea creatures, BUUUUUUUUT

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.440
Having SpongeBob look SO different from his parents

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.220
presents this world with some REAL PROBLEMS.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:29.000
Specifically, whether we can be sure that SpongeBob's parents

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.160
are actually his parents.

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:33.900
In other words, the question we're answering today...

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.720
Was SpongeBob actually adopted?

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.280
Now, I already here some of you down in the comment section,

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:40.740
click-clacking away, saying,

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.860
"Matpat, of course he can't be adopted."

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.500
In episode "Truth or Square",

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.380
we clearly see SpongeBob in Margaret Squarepants's womb

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:51.100
eating Krabby Patties, to which I respond,

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.860
are you even listening to yourself?!

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.740
Seriously! If you watch that episode,

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.360
it's clear that this flashback scene is something that's takes place inside SpongeBob's head!

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:02.680
The idea that SpongeBob would have actual memories dating back to before

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:05.520
he was born is just as ridiculous as the idea that he would be

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.400
chomping on Krabby Patties inside his mother's womb,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:11.580
Which is even less ridiculous than the fact that he is inside his mother's womb at all!

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:14.160
Mainly because sponges don't have wombs!

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.660
Sponge larvae grow and develop outside and apart from their mothers after attaching

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.460
to an underwater surface, like a rock!

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:22.520
So this is not a flashback at all!

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:25.020
This is SpongeBob's imagination hard at work.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.400
Cue that SpongeBob... meme... thing...

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:33.000
SpongeBob: (elongated) "Imagination!"

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.780
This is like... what, number 5 and we're still on page 1?

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.360
HEE HEE! Good thing I front-loaded these things.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.040
Which means that the only way we're gonna prove

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:43.660
SpongeBob's lineage for sure is to look at his family genetics.

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.620
Now, it probably goes without saying that sea sponges are in no way related

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:51.440
to the bright yellow kitchen sponges that form the basis of SpongeBob's design.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:55.260
Those things are just a bunch of cut and formed plastic polymers.

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:59.120
So, in real life there's no way that two sea sponges lookin’ like this,

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.720
would produce something lookin’ like Spongebob.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.220
BUT.

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.620
we can still use the principles of genetics

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.900
and apply them to the rules established within the Bikini-Bottom-verse,

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.180
to determine the probability of SpongeBob being adopted.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:15.480
So let's do like Maury Povich and answer the question,

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.380
"ARE YOU THE FATHER!?"

00:03:17.380 --> 00:03:20.740
And mother... equal opportunity parent... proving.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:24.560
Getting into basics of sponge reproduction, we need to start by asking,

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:27.900
"Do sponges even have fathers and mothers?"

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.400
The answer is yes, sort of...

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:35.480
You see, sponges are just like plants, humans, and most other animals, they reproduce sexually,

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.400
but that doesn't mean you're gonna be traumatized by watching

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.460
two brown blobs rolling around together down in the sea bed.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:41.780
Get it? Sea bed?

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.000
*awkward laugh* Hiiii heyooo!

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.200
That's a "very-safe-for-advertisers" joke.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.360
The only requirement of sexual reproduction is that offspring

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:53.460
be formed by the fusion of two different reproductive cells called gametes.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.940
One coming from the female, the egg and one coming from the male, the sperm.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.720
Sponges actually reproduce the same way plants do.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.225
Plants will release pollen, the male gametes, into the air

00:04:03.225 --> 00:04:08.220
in the hopes that they'll just land on the pistil of the compatible plant nearby and fertilize it.

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:10.000
So if you have seasonal allergies,

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.280
just know that what's making you sneeze is plant sperm.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:14.920
Kinda gross when you actually think about it that way.

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:15.420
*clear fake sneezes from the clip art*

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.800
Sea sponges function in a similar way.

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.580
One sponge releases sperm cells into the water, which are the absorbed by another

00:04:21.580 --> 00:04:25.240
sponge to fertilize its egg.  Except, there's a catch.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.780
Sponges don't come in male and female varieties.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.880
Any sea sponge has the ability to produce both types of

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:36.060
gametes. So while each sponge does have 2 parents, a mother sponge and a father sponge,

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:40.820
It's absolutely possible for a single sponge to be both a father to some baby sponges,

00:04:40.820 --> 00:04:43.200
and a mother to other baby sponges.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:46.740
Which means it's gonna be one awkward birds and bees talk

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.140
with our porous friend Spongebob over here.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:53.020
*In mother voice* "Well, Spongebob, sometimes a mommy sponge just wants to be a daddy sponge

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.980
too." But in all seriousness,

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.780
this "flexible parenting," for lack of a better term,

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:01.940
makes SpongeBob adopting the mother role of the episode, 'Rock-A-Bye Bivalve'

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:03.600
actually make a lot more sense.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.260
So yeah! Sponges do have a father and a mother.

00:05:06.260 --> 00:05:08.880
Each of which contribute genetically to their offspring!

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.000
So we'd expect that the offspring DNA would show the same traits as their parents.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.260
Much in the same way that humans tend to resemble their parents when it comes to things like..

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.520
hair color, eye color, and face shape.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:23.220
But then genetically, is it possible that THESE produced THIS?

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.080
Well, let's put our 6th grade science skills to the test!

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:30.040
Let's see here; the mitochondria is the power house of the cell.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.400
Eh, that's the wrong chapter.

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.400
Mendelian reproduction, peapods

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.100
Ah, yeah there we go.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.400
Our features are determined by genes,

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:39.500
sequences of DNA that encode for specific traits,

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:42.500
and each gene comes in variants called alleles.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:48.420
So, for instance, in the Bikini Bottom universe, you could say that sponges have two different alleles for body shape.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.820
One allele for "Square-Pantsness," and one allele for "Round-Pantsness."

00:05:52.820 --> 00:05:54.420
The same could apply to sponge color,

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:59.340
one allele would be for "Brown Seaspongy color," and another allele would be for "Bright Yellow."

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:05.520
But, in order to explain how two round, brown parents could have a square, yellow child like Spongebob,

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:09.020
we have to look at the relative strength of those alleles.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:11.920
Again, think back to 6th grade. Certain alleles are dominant,

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:13.460
and others are recessive.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.760
Unfortunately, a lot of the examples in humans that you were taught in sixth grade,

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.955
like whether you're right handed or left handed

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.620
or whether you can roll your tongue or not, have been disproven.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.500
They are now lies. They're not just simple dominant-recessive

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.660
relationships anymore. So that kinda left me

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:29.740
with a Pickle Rick about what example I would use to briefly explain this

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:32.340
concept, until I stumbled across...

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:33.900
this new piece of research.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:37.500
You know what human trait has been discovered to be dominant,

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.260
having six fingers.

00:06:39.260 --> 00:06:41.375
Heh-yah, old sixer from Gravity Falls

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.760
is in the dominant category of dactylness.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:50.520
That's how many fingers you have. Yeah, six fingers is dominant over five, I like, quadruple checked it,

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:54.060
and apparently it is a thing, so let's map out these alleles the old fashioned way,

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.305
using a Punnett square.

00:06:55.305 --> 00:06:57.120
Capital letters for dominant traits,

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.480
and lowercase for recessive. So, taking the finger example,

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:05.700
a gene represented by 'FF' would have inherited the dominant allele from both parents,

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.900
and would show six fingers.

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:10.240
A gene represented by 'ff' would have

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:12.820
inherited the recessive allele from both parents,

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.860
and would only have five fingers.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:19.180
And a gene represented by 'Ff' would have inherited the dominant trait from

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:21.300
one parent and the recessive trait from

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:24.020
the other parent, which would still express the dominant trait of

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.900
six fingers, but would carry the potential to

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:29.340
have kids who have five fingers.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:32.555
And if you're ignoring all of this and still wondering how six-fingerness is

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.360
dominant and how more humans don't

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:36.260
have all those extra digits - well,

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:39.600
I'll just leave that one for you to debate in the comments... or research yourself.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.020
Anyway, enough about large-handed humans.

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:45.175
The only way for Spongebob's round, brown parents to

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:47.800
have a yellow square son would be for

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.935
roundness and browness to be the dominant traits

00:07:50.935 --> 00:07:53.565
of sponges in bikini bottom. That would allow

00:07:53.565 --> 00:07:56.135
them to carry the recessive alleles for both

00:07:56.135 --> 00:07:59.235
yellowness and squareness, but still express something

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:02.960
different. So, let's map out Squarepantsness in a Punnett square,

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:04.520
with "R" being roundness and

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:06.955
"r" being squareness. By doing that,

00:08:06.955 --> 00:08:09.225
we see that there are actually 4 possibilities here:

00:08:09.225 --> 00:08:11.860
RR, Rr, rR and rr.

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:15.020
RR and Rr/rR would both show up

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.935
as the dominant trait of roundness, meaning that

00:08:17.935 --> 00:08:20.455
Spongebob has to be a rr,

00:08:20.455 --> 00:08:23.495
which is only one of the four possibilities, so a one

00:08:23.495 --> 00:08:25.755
in four chance of that happening.

00:08:25.755 --> 00:08:28.865
And that's just for him being square! Spongebob would have to have two recessive

00:08:28.865 --> 00:08:31.895
alleles to be yellow as well. That is

00:08:31.895 --> 00:08:34.925
the only way Spongebob wouldn't be adopted in the

00:08:34.925 --> 00:08:37.885
scenario. So it's definitely possible, but

00:08:37.885 --> 00:08:40.535
are these genetic gymnastics really what's going on here?

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:44.220
To double check, we need to see Spongebobs parents and grandparents.

00:08:44.220 --> 00:08:46.515
Unfortunately we can only look at his father's side,

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:49.940
because his mother's half of the family, the Bubble Bottoms, have been surprisingly

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:52.655
ignored across the 11 seasons of the show.

00:08:52.655 --> 00:08:55.485
On Harold's side though, we see Grandma Squarepants

00:08:55.485 --> 00:08:58.285
as another round brown sponge, which makes sense,

00:08:58.285 --> 00:09:01.285
and Grandpa Squarepants as a yellow square.

00:09:01.285 --> 00:09:04.075
Recessive recessive, just like his

00:09:04.075 --> 00:09:06.755
grandson. So running those two

00:09:06.755 --> 00:09:09.875
through a Punnett square, you get a 50/50 split on the kids.

00:09:09.875 --> 00:09:13.065
Half will be round, carrying both a dominant and recessive allele,

00:09:13.065 --> 00:09:15.935
while the other half are totally recessive square. Also,

00:09:15.935 --> 00:09:19.065
half will be brown, again, carrying the dominant-recessive allele

00:09:19.065 --> 00:09:21.960
and the other 50% will be yellow, totally recessive.

00:09:21.960 --> 00:09:25.395
And that is exactly what we see play out

00:09:25.395 --> 00:09:28.075
in the family tree. Spongebob's uncles

00:09:28.075 --> 00:09:30.775
show the exact same mix, Sherm is a yellow

00:09:30.775 --> 00:09:33.775
square, and Blue is a round brown blob.

00:09:33.775 --> 00:09:37.195
So, everything seems to be lining up in our genetic analysis.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:40.160
The science shows that Spongebob isn't adopted.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.800
But there is one last problem here -

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:45.820
the actual odds of all this happening.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:49.040
For parents expressing two dominant traits like Harold and Margaret,

00:09:49.045 --> 00:09:51.505
to have a child expressing two recessive

00:09:51.505 --> 00:09:53.680
traits like Spongebob, the odds are

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:57.515
incredibly low. It's actually 1 in 16,

00:09:57.515 --> 00:10:00.395
which isn't a whole lot. Probability would suggest that

00:10:00.395 --> 00:10:03.385
Harold and Margaret being Spongebob's parents, while,

00:10:03.385 --> 00:10:06.085
yes, plausible, is actually highly unlikely

00:10:06.085 --> 00:10:09.075
to happen. However, when you look across the

00:10:09.075 --> 00:10:12.275
Spongeverse, there's one final genetic quirk

00:10:12.275 --> 00:10:15.295
playing out in Spongebob's favor.

00:10:15.295 --> 00:10:18.345
Sponge color and sponge shape seem to be inherited

00:10:18.345 --> 00:10:20.675
together. Looking across the Spongebob

00:10:20.675 --> 00:10:23.695
family tree, you never see a round yellow sponge

00:10:23.695 --> 00:10:26.605
on the show. NEVER. You also never see

00:10:26.605 --> 00:10:29.425
a square brown sponge, dating all the way

00:10:29.425 --> 00:10:32.195
back to prehistoric times with Primitive Sponge and

00:10:32.195 --> 00:10:34.945
Spongegar. What that tells me is that the traits

00:10:34.945 --> 00:10:38.025
are genetically linked, that the genes dictating these

00:10:38.025 --> 00:10:41.075
two individual traits are close enough

00:10:41.075 --> 00:10:43.475
on the chromosome that getting one most often results

00:10:43.475 --> 00:10:46.265
in you getting the other. Now, there's an entire field of study

00:10:46.265 --> 00:10:49.300
dedicated to this called "genetic mapping", but the TLDR

00:10:49.300 --> 00:10:52.045
of all of this is that it would make the odds of

00:10:52.045 --> 00:10:54.680
Harold and Margaret having a child like Spongebob much closer

00:10:54.680 --> 00:11:00.600
to that 25% the Punnett square revealed, which means that it's much more likely in the realm of believable

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:03.860
possibilities. SPONGEBOB ISN'T ADOPTED.

00:11:03.860 --> 00:11:07.080
At the beginning of the episode, I gave the series creator Stephen Hillenberg

00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:08.760
a lot of credit for bringing

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:11.180
the marine biologist's expertise into

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:14.220
the world of this goofy kids show, but maybe I didn't give him

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:16.720
enough credit. Because in the end, Spongebob

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.100
might look nothing like his parents, but it

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:21.920
doesn't change the fact that when you actually examine the genetics

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:25.860
of the Spongebob family tree, all of it holds up.

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:28.740
As improbable this chain might look at

00:11:28.740 --> 00:11:30.700
first glance, basic genetic science says

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:33.420
that our buddy Spongebob shares a genetic

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.240
link to everyone in it,

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:38.740
even if his parents do look like two cookies.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.080
BUT HEY, THAT'S JUST A THEORY -

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.740
A FILM THEORY. AAAAANNNND

